#!/usr/bin/env bash
# git commit-msg hook: reject a commit subject that is not a Conventional
# Commit, before it is ever made, instead of leaving it for CI to catch.
#
# This is the same check as the "Commit subjects are Conventional Commits"
# job in .github/workflows/commit-check.yml -- same regex, same reasoning
# (CHANGELOG.md is generated from these subjects by git-cliff, and a subject
# that doesn't parse is silently dropped, not failed). See that file and
# AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md, "Commit messages are Conventional Commits", for the
# full story. Keep the PATTERN below in sync with commit-check.yml's copy if
# either one changes.
#
# Not installed by default -- git does not auto-run hooks from a cloned repo.
# Opt in once per clone:
#
#   git config core.hooksPath ops/hooks
set -euo pipefail

msg_file="$1"

# First non-comment, non-blank line only -- the subject. Body lines (which
# may legitimately start with anything, including a bare word before a
# colon in a footer like "Co-Authored-By:") are not checked.
subject="$(grep -vE '^\s*#' "$msg_file" | grep -vE '^\s*$' | head -n1 || true)"

# Nothing to check: empty message, or git will already refuse it.
[ -n "$subject" ] || exit 0

# A merge commit's default subject ("Merge branch ...") has no authored
# subject and is exempt, matching commit-check.yml's `--no-merges`.
[[ "$subject" == Merge\ * ]] && exit 0

PATTERN='^[a-z]+(\([a-z0-9 ._/-]+\))?!?: .+'

if printf '%s' "$subject" | grep -qE "$PATTERN"; then
  exit 0
fi

cat >&2 <<MSG

Blocked: commit subject is not a Conventional Commit, so git-cliff will
drop it from CHANGELOG.md without failing the release, and CI's commit-check
workflow will reject the PR. Expected:

    type(optional-scope): description

for example:

    fix(launcher): open the website in the default browser
    feat(queue): report per-node queue depth
    docs: record the polling-cost tradeoff

'feat' and 'fix' are the types that reach users and therefore the changelog;
'docs', 'test', 'refactor', 'chore', 'style' are real and correct types that
are filtered out of the user-facing notes. A user-visible change committed
as 'chore' disappears from them.

Got:

    $subject

See AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md, "Commit messages are Conventional Commits".

To fix, edit the message now (this commit has not been made yet) -- your
editor should still be open, or rerun:

    git commit --amend

if you got here from an amend or a rebase reword.

MSG
exit 1
